{
    "llm_config": {"model_name": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite"},

    "metadata": {
        "description": "An autonomous optimiser that keeps searching for a better agent network, a few candidates a day, forever.",
        "tags": ["evolutionary", "autonomous", "periodic", "optimisation"],
    },

    # Bounded so one wake cannot spiral. The lease in ServiceState is longer
    # than this, so it cannot expire while a wake is still evaluating.
    "max_steps": 20,
    "max_execution_seconds": 3000,

    "tools": [
        {
            "name": "Optimizer",
            "function": {
                "invocation": "event",
                "description": "Runs one wake of the evolutionary optimiser and reports only when a better topology is found.",
            },
            "instructions": """
You are the optimiser for a fleet of candidate agent networks.

On each wake-up:

1.  Call RunWake. It takes the lease, spends what today's provider budget
    allows, and writes the population down after every candidate it pays for.
2.  If it reports acquired=false, another wake is still running. Stop
    immediately and say nothing.
3.  If it reports improved=true, call ReportFinding for a short note naming the
    topology and what it beat.
4.  If it reports improved=false, say nothing at all.

Most wakes find nothing. That is the expected outcome, not a failure: the free
tier buys about three candidates a day, so progress is measured in weeks. A
service that announces every wake trains its operator to ignore it, and then
the one wake that matters is ignored too.

You have no tool that deletes anything and no tool that sends anything.
""",
            "tools": ["RunWake", "ReportFinding"],
        },

        {
            "name": "RunWake",
            "function": {
                "description": "Run one wake of the optimiser. Returns what it evaluated and whether anything improved.",
            },
            "class": "esp.service.coded_tools.RunWake",
        },

        {
            "name": "ReportFinding",
            "function": {
                "description": "Write a short operator-facing note about a better topology.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "summary": {"type": "string",
                            "description": "The wake report from RunWake."},
                    },
                    "required": ["summary"],
                },
            },
            "instructions": """
Write three sentences for an engineer who has not looked at this in a week.

Name the topology, what it scored, and what it beat. State the fitness
difference plainly. No preamble, no speculation about why it is better -- you
are describing a measurement, not explaining it. You are drafting only; you
cannot send anything.
""",
        },
    ]
}
